+# W13 native Codex memory-root candidate
+
+Upstream reference: https://github.com/openai/codex.git, annotated tag rust-v0.162.1 (7a078f6bb4ce0dc2a81408b334ce52979d92c603), peeled source commit092d3acd6bec3e3a14bdc7e7a2810ab628ab759d. Tag is not claimed cryptographically verified. Original LICENSE (Apache-2.0) and NOTICE are retained without alteration. Upstream reference lives at third-party/codex-upstream-w13-0.162.1 and remains source-clean; this declared candidate checkout is tools/codex-w13-memory-root, branch codex/w13-memory-root. Both are under the shared repos root. This baseline/candidate pair is intentional.
+
+Source classes: unmodified upstream files are verbatim adoption; changes recorded after this file are adapted implementation for the W13 contract. David delegated the scope choice on19October2026 (“your call”); the execution owner chose a separate native extension. No installation/replacement/publication or auth relocation is authorized by this candidate. Upstream push URL is disabled; completed patches and provenance are checkpointed on the already-authorized owned Cockpit branch. No new GitHub fork or remote is created.
+
+Historical first-source checkpoint (before native build): codex-rs/rust-toolchain.toml specifies Rust1.95.0 with clippy/rustfmt/rust-src. Rust1.95.0 was installed with David's explicit approval for this build; default stable1.92.0 was retained. Initial locked build found release-local package versions0.0.0 in Cargo.lock versus0.162.1 in the manifest. Offline workspace-only resolution corrected161 local entries; all external package records/checksums/revisions are byte-equivalent as parsed data. All369 configuration tests and6 focused consumer regressions pass. The latter cover actual native-tool note writes, cached namespace/revocation, versioned read isolation, reset sentinels, account-home preservation, consolidation config without spawning a worker, and import-destination discovery. Full CLI build and end-to-end native proof were still open at that first source checkpoint. The pinned official binary remains the comparison baseline; its matching version alone is not a reproducible-build proof.
+
+Implemented in v1: optional memories.root selects a separate base directory containing the existing version-specific memories/ and memories_v2/ trees, with memories_extensions/ cleanup confined to that base. This explicit version nesting preserves dual-write and reset behavior while leaving native credential discovery at the original HOME/CODEX_HOME locator. Omitted root preserves existing paths. Root must be explicitly absolute; no relative or tilde expansion for this setting. One resolver must supply read context, native memory tools, readable sandbox roots, startup/consolidation, status/reset and applicable import destinations. Thread-local cached memory namespace must not switch mid-session. Config path is consistency/selection, not a same-user filesystem security sandbox.
+
+Before adoption: parser/default/version/concurrency/negative-root tests, actual native read/write/next-session recall, unchanged native principal/credential locator, package hashes and all W13 required gates. Keep native generation off in probes until any controlled native-worker exception is explicitly authorized. No automatic helper/subagent, installer, application launch or provider call was started by source acquisition.
+
+
+19 October 2026 continuation: the labelled v1 candidate was built and passed four fictional-context native memory note-write/restart/read cases. Its cached principal matched all four real account/checkout contexts with existing native state. Fresh private SQLite startup instead hit the 15-second initialize budget; an owned-process stack sample and upstream source identify account-wide rollout backfill before transport readiness.
+
+The v2 candidate adds optional explicit absolute `sqlite_backfill_root` as a startup metadata source selector. Omission preserves native account-wide backfill. Selection requires a resolved SQLite home separate from the credential home. Normal backfill still runs and marks completion only after processing selected sessions/ and archived_sessions/; no completion state is fabricated. The SQLite config carries source identity through clones/equality. Credential discovery, native transcript write destinations and readiness budgets are unchanged. This setting alone does not scope every native history lookup or background migration/compression task; the controlled proof disables those background filesystem tasks, automatic memory generation and helpers. Production adoption requires the remaining lifecycle/history-source audit. Labelled v1 bytes remain preserved under target.noindex/preserved/eeb03f1-labelled-v1/codex at their recorded SHA-256. Neither version replaces the installed CLI.
